WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
OK.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:07.129
Now, I don't want to worry people unnecessarily,
but we need to be correctly concerned, correctly

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:09.860
concerned that national polls have tightened.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:15.330
Donald Trump is closer now to Joe Biden in
national polling than he has been since May,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.060
which was almost five months ago.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.250
These polls, importantly, do not yet take
into account the effect of the first debate.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.850
This is still all predebate polling, but we
have to acknowledge that it is looking less

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:31.620
good for Joe Biden today than it was looking
last month and the month before and the month

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.820
before that.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.550
And if we don't vote, if we don't all vote,
we may all be devastated on November 4th.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.800
So looking at the average of recent national
polling from Real Clear Politics right now,

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.230
Joe Biden's average lead is six point one.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.809
Now, on September 11th, it was eight.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:53.879
And on July 27, that was nine point three.

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:55.700
And on June twenty third, it was ten point
two.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.750
So this is not the right trend.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.460
Now, let's let's look at it in a different
way, in chart form.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.450
So, again, June twenty third.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.760
Biden's up ten point two in the month.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.530
That follows by July 27.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.650
Biden's lead has dropped by just about a point
to nine point three.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.510
By September 11th.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.550
Biden's lead has dropped to eight.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.800
Another roughly point in a half.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:26.770
And then between September 11th and today,
Joe Biden's lead dropped one point nine points

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.640
on average.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.570
This is not good.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:31.640
This is not good.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.790
When you see a lead go from ten point two
to six point one in a few months.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:41.560
That's a 40 percent shrinkage of the lead.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.320
It's not small.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.810
There are also some recent polls that are
not exactly giving me too much comfort.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.950
I've highlighted some of them here on this
image, which we're showing our TV audience.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.280
A recent national poll has Biden only up by
two.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.700
That's the lowest we've seen in a high rated
national poll for a while in Wisconsin.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.950
Joe Biden is only up by two.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.720
That's a state he had been leading by more
on average.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.239
Biden is still winning, but seeing a poll
in which Biden's only up two is not exactly

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:13.540
encouraging.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.170
North Carolina recent poll has Trump ahead
after many polls had Biden ahead.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.379
So this is not panic.

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:23.099
Oh, no.

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:25.830
But it is this is not nearly over.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.530
None of us should think it is.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:34.349
And none of the polls sort of price in voter
